## 2. End-to-End Project Flow

The platform is composed of **seven interconnected modules** that move content from strategy → generation → publishing → measurement → improvement.

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    MOSONIC PLATFORM FLOW                         │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  [ ONE-TIME PER CAMPAIGN ]
        ↓
  ┌─────────────────────┐
  │  1. RULE MODULE     │  ← Strategy input (text, file, URL)
  │  Brand voice, audi- │  ← AI extracts → JSON Rule
  │  ence, goals, chan- │  ← User confirms
  │  nels, keywords     │
  └──────────┬──────────┘
             │  JSON Rule (reusable)
             ↓
  [ PER GENERATION RUN ]
        ↓
  ┌─────────────────────┐
  │  2. WORKFLOW MODULE │  ← User adds Content Prompt
  │  Build pipeline:    │  ← Auto-suggest nodes from Rule
  │  Text → Image →     │  ← User reorders / adds nodes
  │  Translate → Video  │  ← Optional per-node prompts
  └──────────┬──────────┘
             │  Ordered Work Nodes + JSON Rule + Content Prompt
             ↓
  ┌─────────────────────┐         ┌──────────────────┐
  │ 3. ORCHESTRATION    │ ──────→ │ 4. LOGGING       │
  │ Sequential GPT-4o   │  live   │ Real-time stream │
  │ calls per node,     │  logs   │ to frontend, 90- │
  │ pass context fwd    │         │ day retention    │
  └──────────┬──────────┘         └──────────────────┘
             │  Full Content Package
             ↓
  ┌─────────────────────┐
  │  5. CONTENT MODULE  │  ← Draft displayed per node
  │  Edit text inline,  │  ← Re-run any node (with new prompt)
  │  swap image/video,  │  ← Version history kept forever
  │  approve / reject   │
  └──────────┬──────────┘
             │  Approved Content
             ↓
  ┌─────────────────────┐
  │  6. UPLOAD MODULE   │  ← Per-channel preview
  │  Direct or schedule │  ← MCP layer publishes
  │  publish, retry on  │  ← Status tracked per channel
  │  failure            │
  └──────────┬──────────┘
             │  Published Content
             ↓
  ┌─────────────────────┐
  │  7. ANALYTICS       │  ← Weekly auto-pull via MCP
  │  Per-channel metric │  ← Aggregated by Campaign (Rule)
  │  aggregation,       │  ← Auto-feedback suggestions
  │  dashboards         │
  └──────────┬──────────┘
             │  Feedback Signal
             ↓
       [ Loops back to RULE MODULE ]
       Auto-suggested Rule improvements
       → User accepts or rejects
```

### Two Key Architectural Separations

| Separation                                                         | Why It Matters                                                                                                     |
| ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| **Rule** (campaign strategy) vs **Content Prompt** (per-run input) | Strategy stays stable; content varies per run. One Rule fuels many generations.                                    |
| **Node Definition** vs **Pipeline Execution**                      | Workflow stores the template; Pipeline stores the runtime state. Clean separation enables versioning and rollback. |

