## 3. Module 1 — Rule Module

### Purpose

Defines the **strategic foundation** for a campaign — brand voice, audience, goals, channels. Set up **once per campaign** and reused across many generation runs. This is **separate from the content prompt**, which is provided later in the Workflow Module.

### Functionality

**3.1 Strategy Input Handling**
Accepts any of:

- Text, document, or file (PDF, DOCX, TXT) about the business/brand/campaign strategy
- URL — AI scrapes and reads the page (e.g., company website)
- Free text prompt — describing brand or campaign strategy

> ⚠️ This is **NOT the content prompt** — it's about _who the brand is_, not _what to generate_.

**3.2 AI Rule Extraction**
AI reads input **once** and extracts a structured JSON Rule containing:

- Brand tone & voice
- Target audience
- Campaign goals
- Keywords & SEO priorities
- Preferred content formats
- Distribution channels

The original document is stored in MongoDB / S3 as reference.

**3.3 Default Rule Generation**
If user provides no input → system generates a generic baseline JSON Rule so the workflow is never blocked.

**3.4 Rule Review & Confirmation**
User sees the extracted Rule as a readable summary, then confirms or adjusts before saving.

**3.5 Rule Management**

- Save with a name
- Edit field by field
- Duplicate (useful for agencies with multiple clients)
- Delete
- Version history with full snapshot rollback

**3.6 Rule Reusability**
Once saved, the same Rule is reused across many generation runs. Each run only needs a fresh **content prompt** (handled in Workflow Module).

**3.7 Rule Feedback Update**
Analytics sends performance signals back. Rule receives auto-suggested improvements. User accepts or rejects.

### Module Flow

```
[ ONE TIME PER CAMPAIGN ]

User Strategy Input (text / file / URL / prompt about the brand)
        ↓
AI reads input ONCE → Extracts Structured JSON Rule
        ↓
Original doc saved as reference
        ↓
User Reviews & Confirms / Adjusts
        ↓
JSON Rule Saved → reusable across many generation runs
        ↓
Flows into Workflow Module (combined with Content Prompt per run)

[ ONGOING ]
Analytics Feedback → Rule Improvement Suggestion → User Accept/Reject
```

---

## 4. Module 2 — Workflow Module

### Purpose

Builds the **content generation pipeline** for a single generation run. Combines the **Content Prompt** (what to generate this time) with the **JSON Rule** (brand strategy) to drive the work nodes.

### Functionality

**4.1 Content Prompt Input**
User enters the per-run prompt — e.g., _"Write a post announcing our Black Friday 50% off sale"_. This is the **primary input** to the Text Generation node.

**4.2 Predefined Work Node Types**
A fixed set of node types users can pick from:

- 📝 **Text Generation** — always first, cannot be removed (locked)
- 🖼️ **Image Generation** — generates visuals from content context
- 🎬 **Video Generation** — generates video assets
- 🌐 **Translation** — translates generated content into target language

**4.3 Workflow Creation**

- System auto-suggests a workflow based on the JSON Rule (channels, content types)
- User can add extra nodes from the predefined list

**4.4 Work Node Management**

- Insert predefined nodes
- Reorder by drag and drop
- Delete nodes — except Text Generation (locked as first)
- Each node has its own optional prompt input field

**4.5 Node Prompt Input (Optional)**
Each node exposes an editable prompt field. Examples: _"Generate image in minimalist style"_ or _"Translate to Thai, keep formal tone"_. If left empty, the node runs on JSON Rule + Content Prompt + previous outputs.

**4.6 Pipeline Architecture**

```
Content Prompt + JSON Rule
        ↓
[Text Generation Node] (locked, always Node 1)
        ↓ outputs: full generated text
[Image Generation Node] ← consumes text → generates image
        ↓ outputs: text + image
[Translation Node] ← consumes text → translates
        ↓ outputs: text + image + translated text
[Video Generation Node] ← consumes all previous → generates video
        ↓
Final Content Package → Content Module
```

**4.7 Workflow Templates**
Save a configured workflow as a reusable template. Apply across campaigns or clients.

**4.8 Workflow Versioning**
Track changes over time. Roll back to a previous version when needed.

### Key Architectural Points

- **Two combined inputs:** JSON Rule (strategic) + Content Prompt (per-run)
- **Text Generation is always Node 1 and locked** — produces the base content
- **Every subsequent node receives the full output** of the previous node
- **User prompt per node** acts as an extra instruction on top of pipeline context
- **Workflow is per-run** — Rule stays reusable

---

## 5. Module 3 — Orchestration Module

### Purpose

The **execution engine**. Receives the ordered Work Nodes and JSON Rule, then runs the pipeline sequentially while passing context forward and streaming logs live.

### Functionality

**5.1 Pipeline Execution**

- Receives ordered Work Nodes from Workflow Module
- Receives JSON Rule from Rule Module
- Executes nodes **sequentially**, one by one
- Passes the **full output context forward** to each next node

**5.2 Context Building (per node)**
Each node assembles a single AI instruction object containing:

- JSON Rule (tone, audience, goals, keywords)
- User prompt from the node
- Output from all previous nodes

**5.3 Node Execution — GPT Only**
All nodes call **OpenAI GPT-4o**:

| Node                | Backend Call                             |
| ------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| 📝 Text Generation  | GPT-4o LLM                               |
| 🖼️ Image Generation | GPT-4o + DALL-E                          |
| 🌐 Translation      | GPT-4o (translation prompt)              |
| 🎬 Video Generation | GPT-4o + video API (Sora when available) |

**5.4 Live Generation Logging**

- Every node execution writes a real-time log entry to MongoDB
- Logs are streamed to the frontend so the user can watch generation happen live
- Each log captures: node type, input context sent, output received, timestamp, status

**5.5 Retry & Failure Handling**

```
Node Fails
    ↓
Auto Retry Once
    ↓
Still Fails → Pause Pipeline
    ↓
Ask User: Skip this node or Retry manually?
    ├── Skip  → continue without this node's output
    └── Retry → re-run node once more
```

**5.6 Pipeline Status Tracking**
Overall status tracked per execution: `running | completed | failed | paused`.

### Key Decisions

| Decision              | Choice                                        |
| --------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |
| AI Provider           | OpenAI GPT-4o for all nodes                   |
| Generation visibility | Live log streaming to frontend                |
| Retry policy          | Auto retry once, then ask user                |
| On skip               | Pipeline continues without failed node output |

