## 6. Module 4 — Logging Module

### Purpose

Captures and streams generation activity for real-time visibility, debugging, and historical review.

### Functionality

**6.1 Log Capture (Orchestration Only)**
Every node execution writes a log entry capturing:

- Node type
- Short input summary sent to GPT
- Short output summary received
- Timestamp
- Status
- Log level

**6.2 Log Levels**

- **INFO** — normal generation progress (node started, node completed)
- **WARNING** — recoverable unexpected event (retry attempt triggered)
- **ERROR** — node failed after retry, pipeline paused, user action required

**6.3 Log Storage**

- Stored in MongoDB as structured documents
- Linked to pipeline execution ID
- **Auto-deleted after 90 days**

**6.4 Live Log Streaming**
Logs streamed real-time to frontend during generation. Example user view:

```
[INFO]    Text Generation — Started
[INFO]    Text Generation — Completed
[INFO]    Image Generation — Started
[WARNING] Image Generation — Failed, retrying...
[ERROR]   Image Generation — Failed after retry. Action required.
```

**6.5 Failed Node Logs**
Always shows a **short, user-friendly** message — never raw API errors.

✅ Good:

> ❌ Image Generation failed — Could not connect to generation service. Please retry or skip.

❌ Bad:

> ❌ OpenAI API Error 429: Rate limit exceeded on model dall-e-3 at endpoint /v1/images/generations

**6.6 Log History**
User can review logs of any past generation run for 90 days. Useful for understanding why a past generation produced unexpected results.

