## 8. Module 6 — Upload Module

### Purpose

Previews approved content per channel, publishes it directly or on schedule, and tracks status with retry on failure.

### Functionality

**8.1 Receiving Ready Content**
Receives the approved content package from Content Module. Stored as **Ready Content** in MongoDB.

**8.2 Channel Preview (Draft State)**

- Predefined preview templates per channel
- User sees how content will appear on each selected channel before publishing
- Channels selected from the JSON Rule (set during Rule Module)
- Preview adapts content to channel constraints (text length, image ratios, hashtag support, video length)

**8.3 Upload Options**

- **Direct Upload** — publish immediately to selected channels
- **Scheduled Upload** — user picks date and time per channel

**8.4 MCP Layer — Generic Publishing**
A generic MCP endpoint handles actual publishing to all platforms. New platforms added later just need a new preview template — MCP handles the rest.

**8.5 Upload Status Tracking**

- Tracks status per channel: `pending | scheduled | published | failed`
- Notifies user on completion or failure
- Auto-retry on failure

### Channel Templates — Phase 1

| Channel   | Max Text | Image Ratio | Video Support |
| --------- | -------- | ----------- | ------------- |
| Facebook  | 63,206   | 1.91:1      | Yes           |
| Instagram | 2,200    | 1:1 or 4:5  | Yes (60s)     |
| Twitter/X | 280      | 16:9        | Yes (140s)    |
| LinkedIn  | 3,000    | 1.91:1      | Yes           |

### Module Flow

```
Approved Content arrives from Content Module
        ↓
Load channel templates from JSON Rule
        ↓
Show Preview per channel (Draft State)
        ↓
User chooses Direct Upload or Schedule per channel
        ↓
MCP Layer publishes to each channel
        ↓
Track status per channel → Notify user
        ↓
On failure → Retry → Notify user
```

