## 9. Module 7 — Analytics Module

### Purpose

Pulls performance metrics from each platform, aggregates them at the campaign level, and feeds insights back to the Rule Module to continuously improve future content.

### Functionality

**9.1 Performance Data Collection**

- Data pulled **weekly automatically** via MCP Layer from each platform
- Per-channel, per-content metrics: views/impressions, clicks, engagement (likes, shares, comments), conversions

**9.2 Data Aggregation**

- Metrics aggregated at **campaign (Rule) level**
- All content pieces under the same Rule are grouped
- Gives a clear picture of overall campaign performance

**9.3 Dashboard**
Per-campaign metrics and charts:

- Total views / impressions
- Total engagement
- Click-through rate
- Conversions
- Per-channel breakdown
- Filter by **date range** and **campaign (Rule)**

**9.4 Auto Feedback Signal**
After each weekly pull:

- System analyzes performance
- Links results back to the Rule + Workflow that generated the content
- Auto-generates Rule improvement suggestions:
  - Tone adjustments
  - Keyword updates
  - Channel priority changes
- Suggestion sent to Rule Module → user accepts or rejects

### Module Flow

```
Content Published via Upload Module
        ↓
Weekly Auto Pull via MCP Layer
        ↓
Metrics stored per content piece per channel
        ↓
Aggregated at Campaign (Rule) level
        ↓
Dashboard updated with charts & metrics
        ↓
System analyzes performance
        ↓
Auto-generate feedback suggestions
        ↓
Send to Rule Module → User Accept or Reject
```

